From 68751d43c9d6616e54a3b10198c920829f5885b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 05:54:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Loading of the behaviours generated by the generic-parallel
 interface

The libraries generated by the generic-parallel interface of MFront export
functions with the names of the functions of the generic interface, which
integrate batches of integration points. Such a library was loaded without
error and its functions were called with the arguments of a point.

- BehaviourDescription: interface used to generate the behaviour and
  backend of a generic-parallel library, version of the data structures
  checked at loading (isGenericParallelBehaviour);
- Behaviour, initialize functions, post-processings: pointers to the batch
  functions (batch_b, batch_f, batch rotations), the pointers of a point
  being null;
- LibrariesManager: getters of the batch functions, refusal of the
  functions of a point for a generic-parallel library, and conversely;
- BatchDataView.hxx, BatchBehaviourFctPtr.hxx: copies of the data
  structures of the generic-parallel interface (version 2), so that MGIS
  does not depend on TFEL at compile time.

GenericParallelLoadTest checks the loading of a library generated with the
stlpar backend (integration, initialize functions, post-processings,
rotations), the refusals, and the layout of the copied data structures
against the ones of TFEL.
